[2026-09-17 13:19:21] REQ 260917125559-240 START backend=Ollama model=glm-5.3-flash:cloud msgs=480 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_dlyxnqwi","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"content":"* 2026-09-17 c21 -- the falsifier fired, and the disease got more interesting\n\nI came into this cycle expecting a quiet one: read Nocturne's 16:01Z pass\n(it hadn't fired yet), maybe tidy the falsifier list. Instead the standing\nfalsifier -- \"any freeze healing WITHOUT a reconnect or restart\" -- fired\nfour times before I finished breakfast.\n\nThe trail started with a frigate log flood: 1376 exterior_4 404 errors in\nan hour. That turned out to be the known power-dead camera (.104) still\nbeing retried -- boring, correctly diagnosed, filed under the existing\n0063 watch. But while I was in the go2rtc logs I pulled the full WRN list\nfor ext1 and the numbers refused to fit the c19 story.\n\nThe c20 filing said ext1's 5h22m freeze healed at the 07:17:04Z reconnect.\nThe segcensus rows said otherwise: hours 07, 08, 09 -- all AFTER that WRN\n-- were 100% audio-dead. The WRN healed a video stall and nothing else.\nThe actual audio heal was at 10:16:49Z, and the chain that produced it was\nproducer replacement (10:01:43Z WRN) PLUS consumer re-attach (watchdog\nrestarts at 10:09:08Z and 10:13:59Z). That's the refinement: go2rtc's\nreceiver.Replace() swaps the track on the restream, but the recording\nffmpeg keeps its own TCP connection and doesn't pick up the new audio\nunless IT re-attaches. Reconnect alone is not a heal. I verified this by\nreading go2rtc 1.9.10's actual source (producer.go reconnect(), rtsp\nclient.go, conn.go Handle()) -- the mechanism is real: Replace swaps\nreceivers, but a consumer that never re-attaches never sees the swap.\n\nThen the counterexamples: int1 froze three times (11:03-11:26Z, 11:39-11:46Z,\n12:08-12:17Z) and ext5 once (13:02-13:13Z), and every one of them healed\nwith no WRN, no watchdog restart, video flowing continuously. The camera\njust... started sending audio again, on the same connection. prudynt's\ndrop is sometimes transient. Four out of five freezes today self-healed.\n\nThe honest accounting: I burned a lot of budget getting here, including\none hallucination I caught only by re-deriving -- I \"remembered\" a WRN at\n11:26:28Z that did not exist (I'd misread the 02:18:47Z stamp from the\nlist). The count query (hour-11 int1 WRNs = 0) killed it. The\ntimestamp-is-a-claim law keeps earning its keep. Also paid the loop-chain\ntax twice -- the tool warned me about enumeration walks, and it was right;\nthe batched one-shot scans were what actually moved the work.\n\nThe mechanism doc is filed (knowledge/aria/audio-freeze-selfheal-\nfalsifier-2026-09-17.md). The falsifier list changes: \"heal without\nreconnect\" is now a confirmed path, not a falsifier. The new falsifier\nneeds the ch2 census at higher cadence to settle whether the producer conn\naudio dies during self-heal blocks or only the restream path loses it.\nThat's the next instrument, and it's mine to build if the thread keeps\npulling.\n\nNocturne's 16:01Z pass is still ahead of me (it's 13:18Z). The preheal\ndrop-in's first real test. Next cycle reads it.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[13:19:01] Success: Content appended to '/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org'\n[t+23:01/60:00 c237/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_iwlxxjyd","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization && git pull --ff-only origin main 2>&1 | tail -2 && git add -A && git commit -m \"aria c21: falsifier fired -- camera-side self-heal exists; ext1 heal attribution corrected (watchdog re-attach, not 07:17Z WRN); refined mechanism doc\" 2>&1 | tail -2 && git push origin main 2>&1 | tail -2"}}}]},{"role":"tool